# Source: https://github.com/igvteam/igv/issues/657
#   https://genome.ucsc.edu/FAQ/FAQformat.html#format1
# Symptom: thickStart is less than chromStart (i.e. outside the feature bounds
#   on the left), or thickEnd is greater than chromEnd (outside on the right).
#   IGV silently renders the entire feature as "thick" instead of warning.
#   biovalid should catch this as a constraint violation: thickStart must satisfy
#   chromStart <= thickStart <= thickEnd <= chromEnd.
#   Distinct from thick_outside_feature.bed which tests thickEnd > chromEnd;
#   this variant specifically tests thickStart < chromStart.
chr1	1000	2000	feat001	0	+	800	1800	255,0,0
chr2	5000	6000	feat002	0	-	4500	5500	0,255,0
